cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "cliff: Gynecologic Surgical Subspecialty Workforce Cliff Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis and manuscript projecting near-term fellowship-completion
  versus clinical-practice-departure balance, and supply against demographic
  demand, for the United States urogynecology and reconstructive pelvic surgery
  (URPS) and gynecologic oncology workforces. The URPS board-certified-active
  roster and count (1,306 national / 1,303 CONUS, 2023) are produced upstream in
  the isochrones pipeline and served through the mufflyaccess package.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Muffly
    given-names: Tyler
    email: tyler.muffly@dhha.org
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Denver Health Medical Center,
      University of Colorado School of Medicine
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-02"
license: "file LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mufflyt/cliff"
keywords:
  - urogynecology
  - pelvic floor disorders
  - physician workforce projection
  - workforce supply and demand
  - clinical practice departure
  - fellowship training
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Supply and Demand for the United States Urogynecology Workforce, 2025-2050:
    Moving Beyond the Head Count
